{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is undulating.\n    A number is undulating if its digits alternate in a repeating pattern of two distinct digits (d_i = d_{i+2}),\n    and it must have at least three digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_str = str(abs(number))\n\n    if len(number_str) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    d0 = number_str[0]\n    d1 = number_str[1]\n\n    if d0 == d1:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(len(number_str) - 2):\n        if number_str[i] != number_str[i+2]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/88", "solution": "from typing import Any\n\ndef freq_count(input_list: list[Any]) -> dict[Any, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the frequency of each element in a list.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list of elements (can be of any hashable type).\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary where keys are unique elements from the input_list\n        and values are their corresponding frequencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequencies = {}\n    for element in input_list:\n        frequencies[element] = frequencies.get(element, 0) + 1\n    return frequencies"}
