{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "from typing import List, Any, Set\n\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in given nested lists.\n    Returns a set containing elements that are common to all lists within nested_lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize the set of common elements with the elements from the first list\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Intersect with subsequent lists\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        current_list_set = set(nested_lists[i])\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(current_list_set)\n        # Optimization: if common_elements becomes empty, no further intersection is needed\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return common_elements"}
