{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def _rotate_string(s: str, shift_amount: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a string s to the left by shift_amount positions.\"\"\"\n    string_length = len(s)\n    # Ensure shift_amount is within the bounds of string length for cyclic rotation\n    actual_shift = shift_amount % string_length\n    return s[actual_shift:] + s[:actual_shift]\n\ndef _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n    return int(binary_str, 2)\n\ndef _is_odd(decimal_num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a decimal integer is an odd number.\"\"\"\n    return decimal_num % 2 != 0\n\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string\n    the given number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    \n    for i in range(num_rotations):\n        rotated_string = _rotate_string(binary_string, i)\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(rotated_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input conditions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef tuple_to_int(input_tuple: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple of positive integers into a single integer.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if the input is not a tuple or contains non-positive integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    string_parts = []\n    for item in input_tuple:\n        if not isinstance(item, int) or item <= 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"All elements in the tuple must be positive integers.\")\n        string_parts.append(str(item))\n\n    return int(\"\".join(string_parts))"}
