{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef zero_count(numbers: List[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in a given array of integers.\n    Handles edge cases for division by zero by returning float('inf') or float('nan').\n    \"\"\"\n    zero_count = 0\n    non_zero_count = 0\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        if number == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count == 0:\n        if zero_count == 0:  # Empty array\n            return float('nan')\n        else:  # Array with only zeroes\n            return float('inf')\n    else:\n        return zero_count / non_zero_count"}
