{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if element x is a majority element in the sorted array arr of length n.\n\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times. Assumes arr is sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Step 1: Find the first occurrence of x using binary search.\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_occurrence = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            first_occurrence = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # Step 2: If x is not found, return False.\n    if first_occurrence == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Step 3 & 4: Calculate the index of the potential (n/2 + 1)-th occurrence\n    # and check if the element at this calculated index is indeed x.\n    majority_count_needed = n // 2 + 1\n    potential_majority_index = first_occurrence + (majority_count_needed - 1)\n\n    return potential_majority_index < n and arr[potential_majority_index] == x"}
