{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef _get_canonical_form(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple (a, b) to its canonical form (min(a, b), max(a, b)).\"\"\"\n    return (min(t[0], t[1]), max(t[0], t[1]))\n\ndef check_occurences(input_tuples: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"Counts occurrences of canonical tuples in a list.\"\"\"\n    canonical_counts = collections.Counter()\n    for t in input_tuples:\n        canonical_form = _get_canonical_form(t)\n        canonical_counts[canonical_form] += 1\n    return dict(canonical_counts)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(input_integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all odd-indexed bits (0-based from the right) of a given integer to 1.\n    A mask with 1s at all odd positions (1, 3, 5, ...) is generated and then OR-ed with the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_bits_mask = 0\n    # Generate a mask with 1s at odd positions up to a sufficient bit length (e.g., 64 bits).\n    for i in range(1, 64, 2):\n        odd_bits_mask |= (1 << i)\n    result_integer = input_integer | odd_bits_mask\n    return result_integer"}
