{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception to signal invalid input parameters m or n.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total number of valid sequences.\n\n    Args:\n        m: The maximum allowed value for any element in a sequence (positive integer).\n        n: The required length of a sequence (positive integer).\n\n    Returns:\n        The total count of such valid sequences.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If m or n are not positive integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (isinstance(m, int) and m > 0):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"m must be a positive integer.\")\n    if not (isinstance(n, int) and n > 0):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function for recursive sequence counting with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if (current_length, last_element) in memo:\n            return memo[(current_length, last_element)]\n\n        if current_length == n:\n            return 1\n\n        count = 0\n        # The next element must be at least twice the last element and at most m\n        for next_element in range(2 * last_element, m + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element)\n\n        memo[(current_length, last_element)] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_count = 0\n    # The first element can be any value from 1 to m\n    for start_val in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_count += _count_sequences_recursive(1, start_val)\n\n    return total_count\n```"}
