{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\n\n    Returns the smallest perfect square (an integer) strictly greater than the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the square root of the input number.\n    sqrt_val = math.sqrt(number)\n\n    # Determine the next integer root by taking the floor of the square root and adding 1.\n    # This works for both perfect squares (e.g., sqrt(36)=6, next_root=7)\n    # and non-perfect squares (e.g., sqrt(35)=5.9..., floor=5, next_root=6).\n    next_int_root = int(sqrt_val) + 1\n\n    # Square this next integer root to get the result.\n    return next_int_root * next_int_root"}
