{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence first increases and then decreases.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Initialize LIS_sum array\n    # lis_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    lis_sum = list(arr) \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Initialize LDS_sum array\n    # lds_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i\n    lds_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS_sum and LDS_sum to find the maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Subtract arr[i] once because it's included in both lis_sum[i] and lds_sum[i]\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
