{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_input(n: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates if n is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    _validate_input(n)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize for L(0) and L(1)\n    a, b = 2, 1\n    # Calculate iteratively from L(2) up to L(n)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_lucas\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given integer 'n' using the recursive formula:\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    All divisions are integer divisions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        _memo[n] = n\n        return n\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
