{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Modifies the input list in-place and returns it.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\n\ndef and_tuples(tuple1: Tuple[int, ...], tuple2: Tuple[int, ...]) -> Tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an element-wise bitwise AND operation on two input tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first input tuple, containing integer elements.\n        tuple2: The second input tuple, containing integer elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the results of the element-wise bitwise AND operations.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input tuples have different lengths.\n        TypeError: If any element in the input tuples is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        element1 = tuple1[i]\n        element2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(element1, int) or not isinstance(element2, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input tuples must be integers.\")\n\n        result_elements.append(element1 & element2)\n\n    return tuple(result_elements)"}
