{"task_id": "Mbpp/447", "solution": "class Number:\n    \"\"\"Represents a numerical value and provides the operation to cube itself.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Number value must be an integer.\")\n        self._value = value\n\n    def cube(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the cube of the number's value.\"\"\"\n        return self._value * self._value * self._value\n\ndef cube_nums(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the cube of each individual element in an input list.\n    Returns a new list containing the cubed values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    cubed_list = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        number_obj = Number(num)\n        cubed_list.append(number_obj.cube())\n\n    return cubed_list"}
