{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(int1: int, int2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the absolute differences between corresponding digits of two integers.\n    Pads shorter numbers with leading zeros to match length.\n    \"\"\"\n    s1 = str(int1)\n    s2 = str(int2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(s1), len(s2))\n\n    s1_padded = s1.zfill(max_len)\n    s2_padded = s2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_difference = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(s1_padded[i])\n        digit2 = int(s2_padded[i])\n        total_difference += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_difference"}
