{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1: list[int], array2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth smallest element from two sorted arrays.\n    Handles validation for k and combines elements efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a positive integer.\")\n    total_length = len(array1) + len(array2)\n    if k > total_length:\n        raise ValueError(\"k is greater than the total number of elements.\")\n\n    # Two-pointer approach to find the kth element without fully merging\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    while True:\n        if i == len(array1):\n            return array2[j + k - 1]\n        if j == len(array2):\n            return array1[i + k - 1]\n\n        if k == 1:\n            return min(array1[i], array2[j])\n\n        # Optimize search range if k is large\n        mid = k // 2\n        new_i = min(i + mid, len(array1))\n        new_j = min(j + mid, len(array2))\n\n        if array1[new_i - 1] <= array2[new_j - 1]:\n            k -= (new_i - i)\n            i = new_i\n        else:\n            k -= (new_j - j)\n            j = new_j"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is one where the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the total number of digits, equals the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    original_num = num\n    num_str = str(num)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n    sum_of_powers = 0\n\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return sum_of_powers == original_num"}
