{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(array: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the order of elements in the input array from the beginning\n    up to the k-th position (1-indexed).\n    \"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = k - 1\n    while left < right:\n        array[left], array[right] = array[right], array[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return array"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/722", "solution": "```python\ndef filter_data(students_data: dict[str, tuple[float, float]], minimal_height: float, minimal_weight: float) -> dict[str, tuple[float, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters students based on height and weight criteria.\n\n    Returns a dictionary of students whose height and weight meet or exceed the minimums.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_students = {}\n    for name, (height, weight) in students_data.items():\n        if height >= minimal_height and weight >= minimal_weight:\n            filtered_students[name] = (height, weight)\n    return filtered_students\n```"}
