{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list by a specified number of items to the right direction.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(positions, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"positions must be an integer\")\n\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_positions = positions % list_length\n\n    rotated_list = input_list[list_length - effective_positions:] + input_list[:list_length - effective_positions]\n\n    return rotated_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "def capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before uppercase letters in a string, excluding the first character.\n    Returns a new string with added spaces for improved readability.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result = [input_string[0]]  # Start with the first character\n\n    for char in input_string[1:]:  # Iterate from the second character\n        if char.isupper():\n            result.append(\" \")\n        result.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result)"}
